  "capture_notes": [
   "two consecutive runs produced byte-identical output",
   "random approval ids, shred ids and approval tickets are replaced by <approvalId>, <shredId> and <ticket12>; the first 12 hex digits of the latest checkpoint root by <root12>; bodies carrying them are reduced to response_keys plus the named fields",
   "records lists hold the audit records appended by one exchange, reduced to event_type, actor_kind, tenant_id, route_class, verdict, action, mode, fail_reason and key_id",
   "execute_at_minus_now_in is executeAtUnix minus the wall-clock Unix seconds read just after and just before the commit request",
   "executesInSec is read by a list request issued immediately after the commit, so the elapsed time is a small fraction of a second",
   "banStack seals a checkpoint every 8 records; the hold-window stack had 8 records (tree_size 8) when RunDueShreds ran and the no-subject stack had fewer (no checkpoint)"
  ],
  "scope": "Frozen oracle outputs for differential parity only; never regenerate to hide drift"
